<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Ndzundza Ndebele Kingdom</h1><p class="st-meta">1650 CE – 1883 CE (approx.) · capital KwaMaza</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Southern Ndebele kingdom of the eastern Transvaal that held out against the Boers from its cave fortress until 1883.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ndebele-kingdom">Ndebele</a> tradition says the Ndzundza branch split from the senior Manala house after a dispute among the sons of the ruler Musi in the 17th century. The Ndzundza settled east of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pretoria">Pretoria</a> and later established a stronghold at KwaMaza near modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roossenekal">Roossenekal</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The king ruled through royal kin and regimental age-sets, and the kingdom recovered from defeat by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mzilikazi">Mzilikazi</a> in the 1820s under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mabhoko">Mabhoko</a> (Mapoch), who used the caves of KwaMaza as a defensive refuge. Ndzundza homesteads were later noted for their striking painted walls and women's beadwork, which became emblems of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ndebele-kingdom">Ndebele</a> identity.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1882 King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nyabela">Nyabela</a> sheltered the Pedi rebel <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mampuru-ii">Mampuru</a>, and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/south-african-republic">South African Republic</a> besieged KwaMaza. After a long siege the Ndzundza surrendered in 1883; their land was confiscated and the people indentured to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boers">Boer</a> farmers.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1650 CE – 1883 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Central and Southern Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:92.54%;width:4.64%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1650 CE – 1883 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>KwaMaza</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Mabhoko, Nyabela</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Traditional Ndebele religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>isiNdebele (Southern)</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/south-africa">South Africa</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Ndzundza, Southern Ndebele, Mapoch</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1766&amp;focus=ndzundza-ndebele-kingdom" aria-label="Ndzundza Ndebele Kingdom on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5310 3268 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Ndzundza Ndebele Kingdom lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5746 3380h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5630 3524h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5630 3524h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day South Africa. <a href="/atlas?year=1766&amp;focus=ndzundza-ndebele-kingdom">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

